      "writtenOn": "2025-07-07T21:29:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Agree, pushed another patch-set with the comments incorporated",
      "parentUuid": "7f11bb16_a43fb4ac",
      "revId": "ffd1c18811a50d7d96a4b9198f4d2a44265d85f0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "732d7fd6_5cde1f48",
        "filename": "drivers/iommu/intel/iommu.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 3064,
      "author": {
        "id": 1015280
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-07-04T01:11:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Shall the ATC_REQUIRED flag being checked here? My understanding is that, if ATC_REQUIRED flag is not set, it means we don\u0027t need to enable the device IOTLB for the devices covered by this STAC table (suppose we don\u0027t need to look into the device scope to query the ATC_REQUIRED for each device). Is this a correct understanding?\n\nAnother question is that, for an IOMMU, if one of its device is listed in the SATC, then this IOMMU will be marked have device iotlb ecap, then the pkvm hypervisor will not clear the DTE from the context entry for any device in this IOMMU. This sounds like an overfit?",
      "revId": "ffd1c18811a50d7d96a4b9198f4d2a44265d85f0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3abb526f_d2c45698",
        "filename": "drivers/iommu/intel/iommu.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 3064,
      "author": {
        "id": 4168684
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-07-04T01:59:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "1) Correct, I missed the check on ATC_REQUIRED. I will add that.\n2) I am not sure about what would happen if the context entry DTE is cleared even if device is listed to have an ATC. Are you suggesting the check for clearing the DTE in the context entry be removed?",
      "parentUuid": "732d7fd6_5cde1f48",
      "revId": "ffd1c18811a50d7d96a4b9198f4d2a44265d85f0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "248b987e_0079e76f",
        "filename": "drivers/iommu/intel/iommu.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 3064,
      "author": {
        "id": 1015280
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-07-04T02:21:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The overfit I mean is like what I mentioned in another comment:\n\"with this patch, for example, if an IOMMU contains two devices, device A is described by the SATC, but the device B is not. Then seems this patch will set the DT bit for this IOMMU. And the pkvm hypervisor will enable device iotlb for both device A and device B, but in fact, we only want the device A to have device iotlb as device B is not described in the SATC.\"\n\nPlease correct me if I am wrong about this.",
      "parentUuid": "3abb526f_d2c45698",
      "revId": "ffd1c18811a50d7d96a4b9198f4d2a44265d85f0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a293e7c4_77577dfa",
        "filename": "drivers/iommu/intel/iommu.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 3064,
      "author": {
        "id": 4168684
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-07-04T04:31:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Similar to my response above, as per the PTL spec only 4 devs (IGD, NPPU, IPU, PMCS) have devTLB and Intel HW guarantees security of all those 4 dev. So even if they are not listed in SATC, enabling ECAP.DT for that remapping unit should be okay.",
      "parentUuid": "248b987e_0079e76f",
      "revId": "ffd1c18811a50d7d96a4b9198f4d2a44265d85f0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "89d010e6_65509dc6",
        "filename": "drivers/iommu/intel/iommu.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 3064,
      "author": {
        "id": 1015280
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-07-04T05:35:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for checking the PTL\u0027s design. So seems implementing like this is fine to PTL. What in my mind is to enable device iotlb for the device if it is in the SATC table. The host IOMMU driver can provide an interface for the pkvm_host.c to check if a pci device is in a SATC with ATC_REQUIRED \u003d\u003d 1. The pkvm_host.c can check for each pci device and collect a array which contains the BDF of the pci device in such SATC for the pkvm hypervisor. Then the pkvm iommu driver can enable the device iotlb for a pci device if its BDF is in this array.\n\nI guess we will prefer to have a more general way to enable device iotlb in the pvIOMMU solution. If this patch is just for the emulated-based IOMMU, probably it is fine.",
      "parentUuid": "a293e7c4_77577dfa",
      "revId": "ffd1c18811a50d7d96a4b9198f4d2a44265d85f0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e16b9c2b_396f1a49",
        "filename": "drivers/iommu/intel/iommu.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 3064,
      "author": {
        "id": 2022314
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-07-04T19:24:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Regarding ATC_REQUIRED, actually I suppose it is not necessary to check it. If I\u0027m reading VT-d spec correctly, all SoC-integrated devices that use ATS (even if they don\u0027t absolutely require it) are required to use it in a secure way (section 4.4: \"The Figure 4-3 below shows a typical SoC integrated device that is connected to the Root Complex. All\nsuch devices that support Address Translation Service (ATS) must create an isolation boundary\noutside of which Host Physical Address (HPA) are not exposed. ...\")\n\nSo if we assume that all devices listed in SATC are trusted to use ATS securely, why not allow it even for those of them which don\u0027t have ATC_REQUIRED, to let them enjoy better performance?",
      "parentUuid": "89d010e6_65509dc6",
      "revId": "ffd1c18811a50d7d96a4b9198f4d2a44265d85f0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2e2d493d_a0eafdc4",
        "filename": "drivers/iommu/intel/iommu.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 3064,
      "author": {
        "id": 4168684
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-07-07T21:29:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In the latest patchset I have checked for ATC_required, I agree that any device on the list should be allowed to enjoy the better performance. Should the keep be removed ?",
      "parentUuid": "e16b9c2b_396f1a49",
      "revId": "ffd1c18811a50d7d96a4b9198f4d2a44265d85f0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
